<section class="py-8 sm:py-16 lg:py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <!-- FAQ Header -->
    <div class="mb-12 space-y-4 text-center sm:mb-16 lg:mb-24">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold md:text-3xl lg:text-4xl">
        Need Help? We've Got Answers
      </h2>
      <p class="text-xl">
        Explore Our Most Commonly Asked Questions and Find the Information You
        Need.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div
      class="w-full divide-y"
      x-data="{ open: 'upgrade' }"
    >
      <div>
        <button
          type="button"
          id="upgrade"
          class="inline-flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-4 text-start font-medium"
          x-on:click="open = open === 'upgrade' ? null : 'upgrade'"
          x-bind:aria-expanded="(open === 'upgrade').toString()"
          aria-controls="upgrade-collapse"
        >
          Do you charge for each upgrade?
          <span
            class="icon-[tabler--plus] size-4.5 shrink-0"
            x-show="open !== 'upgrade'"
          ></span>
          <span
            class="icon-[tabler--minus] size-4.5 shrink-0"
            x-cloak
            x-show="open === 'upgrade'"
          ></span>
        </button>
        <div
          id="upgrade-collapse"
          class="w-full overflow-hidden"
          aria-labelledby="upgrade"
          role="region"
          x-show="open === 'upgrade'"
          x-collapse
        >
          <div class="px-5 pb-4">
            <p>
              Lemon drops chocolate cake gummies carrot cake chupa chups muffin
              topping. Sesame snaps icing marzipan gummi bears macaroon dragée
              danish caramels powder. Bear claw dragée pastry topping soufflé.
              Wafer gummi bears marshmallow pastry pie
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <button
          type="button"
          id="license-website"
          class="inline-flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-4 text-start font-medium"
          x-on:click="open = open === 'license-website' ? null : 'license-website'"
          x-bind:aria-expanded="(open === 'license-website').toString()"
          aria-controls="license-website-collapse"
        >
          Do I need to purchase a license for each website?
          <span
            class="icon-[tabler--plus] size-4.5 shrink-0"
            x-show="open !== 'license-website'"
          ></span>
          <span
            class="icon-[tabler--minus] size-4.5 shrink-0"
            x-cloak
            x-show="open === 'license-website'"
          ></span>
        </button>
        <div
          id="license-website-collapse"
          class="w-full overflow-hidden"
          aria-labelledby="license-website"
          role="region"
          x-cloak
          x-show="open === 'license-website'"
          x-collapse
        >
          <div class="px-5 pb-4">
            <p>
              Yes, you need to purchase a separate license for each website
              where you plan to use our components. Each license is tied to a
              single domain and its subdomains. This ensures proper licensing
              compliance and helps us maintain and improve our products for all
              users.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <button
          type="button"
          id="regular-license"
          class="inline-flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-4 text-start font-medium"
          x-on:click="open = open === 'regular-license' ? null : 'regular-license'"
          x-bind:aria-expanded="(open === 'regular-license').toString()"
          aria-controls="regular-license-collapse"
        >
          What is regular license?
          <span
            class="icon-[tabler--plus] size-4.5 shrink-0"
            x-show="open !== 'regular-license'"
          ></span>
          <span
            class="icon-[tabler--minus] size-4.5 shrink-0"
            x-cloak
            x-show="open === 'regular-license'"
          ></span>
        </button>
        <div
          id="regular-license-collapse"
          class="w-full overflow-hidden"
          aria-labelledby="regular-license"
          role="region"
          x-cloak
          x-show="open === 'regular-license'"
          x-collapse
        >
          <div class="px-5 pb-4">
            <p>
              A regular license grants you the right to use our components on a
              single website or project. It includes access to all basic
              features, documentation, and standard support. This license is
              perfect for individual developers or small businesses working on a
              single project.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <button
          type="button"
          id="extended-license"
          class="inline-flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-4 text-start font-medium"
          x-on:click="open = open === 'extended-license' ? null : 'extended-license'"
          x-bind:aria-expanded="(open === 'extended-license').toString()"
          aria-controls="extended-license-collapse"
        >
          What is extended license?
          <span
            class="icon-[tabler--plus] size-4.5 shrink-0"
            x-show="open !== 'extended-license'"
          ></span>
          <span
            class="icon-[tabler--minus] size-4.5 shrink-0"
            x-cloak
            x-show="open === 'extended-license'"
          ></span>
        </button>
        <div
          id="extended-license-collapse"
          class="w-full overflow-hidden"
          aria-labelledby="extended-license"
          role="region"
          x-cloak
          x-show="open === 'extended-license'"
          x-collapse
        >
          <div class="px-5 pb-4">
            <p>
              An extended license provides additional rights and features beyond
              the regular license. It includes usage rights for multiple
              websites, priority support, access to premium components, and the
              ability to use components in commercial projects that you sell to
              end customers. Perfect for agencies and large enterprises.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
